<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 1</h2>
<p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 37.5%;"><b>Scenario:</b> It's the Rainy Season</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 37.5%;"><b>Theme:</b> I Need an Umbrella.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Engage in simple exchanges about familiar topics.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can identify the setting and characters in simple audio stories about rain (e.g., 'The story is about a boy with an umbrella.').<br>Can join in simple exchanges about rainy days (e.g., 'What do you wear in the rain?' 'I wear boots.').<br>Can answer questions about rainy day items (e.g., 'What do you need?' 'I need an umbrella.').</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher greets students and asks, "What's the weather like today?" The teacher shows a large picture of a rainy day with children wearing raincoats and boots, and holding umbrellas, while splashing in puddles. The teacher plays a short audio clip of rain sounds. Teacher asks, "What sounds do you hear?" "What season is it?" "What do we need when it rains?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher holds up realia (an umbrella, a small raincoat, a boot) and flashcards for 'umbrella', 'raincoat', 'boots', 'puddle'. The teacher clearly models the pronunciation of each word, focusing on /r/ in 'rain' and /p/ in 'puddle'. The teacher points to a picture of rain and says, "It is raining. I need an umbrella." The teacher mimes putting on a raincoat and says, "I wear a raincoat." The teacher models spelling 'raincoat' and 'muddy' orally.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Showing an umbrella) "Is this for sunny days or rainy days?" (Expected answer: "Rainy days!")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Pointing to a picture of boots) "Do I wear sandals or boots in a puddle?" (Expected answer: "Boots!")</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(8-10 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "It's the Rainy Season"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio story (narrative excerpt/dialogue) about two children getting ready for a rainy day. The audio includes sentences like: "It is raining outside! Look at the big puddles! I need my raincoat and my boots. Do you need an umbrella, Leo? Yes, I need an umbrella. Let's go splash in the puddles!"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Engage in simple exchanges about familiar topics and narrate current events related to weather using the present continuous tense.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Listening for gist and specific information):</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher plays the audio once. <b>Gist Question:</b> "Who is talking in the story? Is it two boys, two girls, or a boy and a girl?" (Students listen and raise hands for their answer). "What are they talking about?" (Students listen and say "rainy day" or "rain").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher plays the audio again. <b>True/False Questions:</b> The teacher holds up True/False cards. "The story is about a sunny day." (False). "The boy needs a raincoat." (False - only the girl). "They want to splash in puddles." (True).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher plays the audio a third time, pausing. <b>Information Matching:</b> Students listen and point to flashcards on the board for 'umbrella', 'raincoat', 'boots', 'puddle' as they hear the words.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(10-12 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Listening for specific vocabulary (umbrella, raincoat, boots, puddle, wet, muddy), grammar (Present Simple: 'I need...', 'I wear...'; Present Continuous: 'It is raining...'), and WH-questions ('What do you need?', 'What do you wear?').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                        <ol>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listen and Draw (Controlled Practice):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with three empty boxes. The teacher says three sentences, one for each box: "1. I need a yellow umbrella." "2. It is raining. I wear my red boots." "3. I like to splash in big puddles." Students listen carefully and draw what they hear in each box. The teacher repeats each sentence twice.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listen and Point (Semi-controlled Practice):</b> The teacher displays flashcards for 'raincoat', 'sandals', 'boots'. The teacher says sentences, and students listen and point to the correct flashcard. E.g., "It is raining! I wear my... (pause) ...boots!" "It is sunny. I wear my... (pause) ...sandals!" "When it pours, I need a... (pause) ...raincoat!"</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listen and Match (Pair Check):</b> In pairs, students receive a worksheet with pictures of rainy day items (umbrella, raincoat, boots, muddy puddle) and a short phrase bank (e.g., 'keeps you dry', 'splash in it', 'for your feet', 'for your body'). One student reads a phrase aloud, and their partner listens and points to the matching picture. Then they swap roles.</li>
                        </ol>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(12-15 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "It's the Rainy Season"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Task Format:</b> "Rainy Day Needs" Listening Game.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher plays different short audio clips:
                        <ol>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sound of heavy rain and thunder.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sound of light rain.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sound of children splashing in puddles.</li>
                        </ol>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">After each sound clip, the teacher asks the class (choral response encouraged): "What do you need?" or "What do you wear?" Students listen to the sounds and the question, and respond with appropriate vocabulary. E.g., for heavy rain/thunder: "I need an umbrella!" "I need a raincoat!" For splashing: "I wear boots!" "I want to puddle-jump!" This encourages active listening and simple, immediate verbal responses.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher gives simple prompts: "It is raining. I am wet. What do I need?" (Students listen and say "An umbrella!") "The puddles are muddy. What do I wear?" (Students listen and say "Boots!")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Focus on listening to the prompt and producing simple, correct answers using target vocabulary.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(8-10 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> "Listen and Circle." The teacher distributes a worksheet with pictures of items (e.g., umbrella, sun, raincoat, shorts, boots, sandals) in rows. The teacher reads a short sentence for each row (e.g., "1. When it is rainy, I need an umbrella." "2. It is raining. I wear my boots." "3. I am wearing my raincoat because it is pouring."). Students listen and circle the correct item in each row.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accuracy of identification: Student correctly circles the described item.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Comprehension of instructions: Student follows directions to listen and circle.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of target vocabulary (if applicable for any verbal response given by student).</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer two questions on a small slip of paper before leaving:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What new words about rain did I learn today? (e.g., "umbrella," "puddle")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can I understand when someone talks about what they need for a rainy day? (Yes/No/A little)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5-7 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was easy for me when listening to the rainy day stories and questions today?</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was difficult for me when listening today, and why?</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The listening activities were effective in introducing new vocabulary and concepts. The students responded well to the audio story and sound effects. Some students struggled with differentiating between 'raincoat' and 'umbrella' in faster speech, requiring more modeling of /r/ sounds. I need to ensure clear pronunciation and repetition for these phonemes in future lessons.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 2 (Reading Comprehension), students will engage with a short illustrated text using the same vocabulary words (umbrella, raincoat, boots, puddle, wet, muddy) to reinforce their understanding of the context and meaning.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(2-3 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>